**Company Description**  

Amsterdam \| 6 months


Are you looking for an internship where you can work independently, take charge of projects, and make a direct impact? Flink is looking for a **Marketing Intern (m/f/d)**, who is ready to take true ownership and thrives in a dynamic, results\-driven environment.


You will join the marketing team at our Amsterdam HQ, contributing to strategic campaigns and initiatives. From day one, you will drive independent projects and support colleagues at both national and local (hub) levels. This includes managing campaigns, conducting competitor analyses, and coordinating cross\-functional initiatives with other teams.


You will play an active role in our campaigns, taking responsibility for uploading and quality\-checking in\-app banners and stories. Additionally, you will engage our massive customer base by deploying weekly push notifications and emails to maximize campaign impact.

 **Job Description**  

* Campaign Execution: Support the rollout and optimization of marketing campaigns and targeted local initiatives at the hub level;
* Content Management: Ensure the quality, accuracy, and perfect timing of all visual content, such as banners and stories, within the Flink app;
* Customer Activation: Drive conversions by testing and launching weekly email and push notification campaigns to hundreds of thousands of users;
* End\-to\-End Project Management: Drive projects from briefing to completion, managing deadlines and ensuring flawless delivery;
* Data\-Driven Optimization: Dive into campaign metrics to identify what works, translating data into actionable insights for improvement;
* Team Player: Actively participate in team meetings and contribute creative ideas to elevate our marketing strategy.


This position requires being in the office at least 3\-4 days per week (we do not provide compensation for travel costs).

 **Qualifications**  

* You love working independently and feel comfortable taking on responsibility;
* You thrive in a fast\-paced environment and can switch gears quickly;
* You have a proactive attitude—you spot opportunities and bring ideas to the table;
* You are analytical, structured, and possess a sharp eye for detail;
* You have excellent communication skills in both Dutch and English (written and spoken);
* You are looking for a voluntary internship (at the moment, we are not able to provide support with mandatory internships);
* You are currently pursuing a relevant Bachelor's or Master’s degree (e.g., Marketing, Business Administration, or Commercial Economics).



**Additional Information**  

The following starting salary applies to this position as a **Marketing Intern (m/f/d)**:


The base salary for this position is €500\.00 for Bachelor's students and €800\.00 for Master's students, gross per month based on full\-time (40 hours per week). In addition, Flink offers the following benefits:

* Plenty of room for initiative and working independently on real projects;
*

Come reimagine hospitality with us as our new superhost of our Amsterdam West location!


**Your mission should you choose to accept it…**



As our Front Office Intern, you'll be operating in all of our front of house areas, making sure that each guest is having the best possible TSH\-experience. Whether you're providing a flawless welcome and check in, awesome service in our restaurant and bars or just having a chat to make their stay truly unforgettable ― you are at the forefront of our guest facing operation. You know everything about our products and how to (cross\-)sell these to our guests. And it's because of you that everyone who enters our Amsterdam\-location will become a raving fan of TSH instantly!


**In case you don't know who we are:**



Known for being the rule breakers in hospitality, TSH is a fun, creative and inspiring environment where everyone can work, stay, learn and play and most importantly – be themselves. As an employer we look, act and think like a hotel, but instead we offer a lot more. Think student accommodation, long and short stay options, gyms, talks, events, rooftop bar and eat \& drink escapes as well as community and coworking spaces. Located in The Netherlands, Germany, Austria, Italy, France and Spain with several new openings on the way, this hybrid hospitality concept may take root in the heart of Europe, but our plans are set for going global.


**What You'll Do**


* You make sure everyone gets a warm welcome as soon as they walk in;
* You'll help our guests at our reception desk.
* You'll be a secret concierge to the city, answering all of your guests' questions about the best places to visit, eat, shop or party;
* Tidy home's a happy home. You'll make sure everything is spick and span in all areas and ready for the following shift;
* You'll help our guests with any requests or demands regarding our facilities (you may even pick up some new tech skills along the way!).


**Who You Are**


* You're currently enrolled in a University;
* Currently studying a relevant bachelor's in Hospitality, Sales, Advertising, Marketing, or Business;
* Enjoy receiving and taking responsibility and you can work independently;
* You have a flexible, hands\-on, motivated and positive approach;
* You're an octopus that loves to get your dexterity skills into action;
* You love responsibility and handle stressful peak periods like a pro;
* Fluent in English and Dutch – Know any other languages? The more the merrier!
* Hard working, responsible and a "let's do this!" mentality;
* You must be studying within the EU.


**What We Offer**


* An amazing work environment with a fantastic vibe and lots of positive energy.
* On the job coaching and guidance.
* Monthly compensation for your internship.
* The opportunity to work and learn at a dynamic, young, international organisation; we're a real game changer in the hospitality industry.
